# Production Readiness Guide: Razorpay Payment Integration (Node.js + React)

This document lists what is required, and what must be changed, before the Razorpay payment feature is deployed to production.

---

## 1. Current State vs. Production Requirement

| Area | Practice Code | Required in Production |
|---|---|---|
| Razorpay keys | Test mode keys | Live mode keys, after Razorpay account activation (KYC and business verification) |
| Transport | HTTP on localhost | HTTPS only |
| Webhook | Not reachable from the internet | Public HTTPS webhook URL registered in the Razorpay dashboard |
| Secrets | Plain `.env` file | Host-level environment variables or a secret manager |
| Fulfilment | Status saved as `paid` only | Business action (access, delivery, invoice) triggered once per payment |
| Amount check | Signature verified only | Signature plus amount and currency cross-check |
| Duplicate events | Handled by status check | Handled by event-id deduplication |
| Stuck orders | Remain `created` forever | Reconciliation job |
| Refunds | Not implemented | Refund flow with audit trail |
| Rate limiting | None | Enabled on payment routes |
| Logging | `console.log` | Structured logs, alerts on payment failures |
| Legal pages | None | Terms, privacy policy, refund and cancellation policy |